WEBVTT

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.260
Meth? Why is a man like him...

00:02:10.260 --> 00:02:12.260
There's no question about it.

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.850
He's the only member of the
Council in Japan right now.

00:02:16.030 --> 00:02:19.990
So, they're after Yushiro and Miharu?

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:26.500
Yushiro used to be part of
the Gowa Group.

00:02:27.770 --> 00:02:30.610
Is weapons development the
common denominator here?

00:02:30.610 --> 00:02:32.510
But why go through
all this just for...

00:02:33.250 --> 00:02:35.340
Damn, game over.

00:02:44.560 --> 00:02:46.330
Good morning.

00:02:46.330 --> 00:02:47.630
Today's top story is a follow up

00:02:47.630 --> 00:02:51.400
on the riots that erupted yesterday
in the northern Kanto region.

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:54.800
Late last night, two police officers
were injured as a result

00:02:54.800 --> 00:02:59.070
of the riots that once again erupted
in the Asian Veins.

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:01.340
At least five illegal immigrants
have been reported killed

00:03:01.340 --> 00:03:04.440
as a result of these violent
clashes with the police.

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.610
The police also report...

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:05.940
Yes, I've been informed about it.
The police also report...

00:03:05.940 --> 00:03:08.670
Yes, I've been informed about it.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:12.350
Have you been able to gather more
information on the group

00:03:12.350 --> 00:03:13.850
that is protecting Yushiro?

00:03:13.850 --> 00:03:17.660
It seems it is an organization
known as the Kyouwakai.

00:03:17.660 --> 00:03:18.760
The Kyouwakai?

00:03:18.760 --> 00:03:19.160
Yes, it's a mutual cooperative made up
of residents of the Asian Veins
The Kyouwakai?

00:03:19.160 --> 00:03:22.660
Yes, it's a mutual cooperative made up
of residents of the Asian Veins

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:25.400
which conducts neighborhood patrols
and armed defense operations.

00:03:25.400 --> 00:03:28.030
In actuality, they are
like a mafia group.

00:03:28.030 --> 00:03:30.840
I've been informed that, because of
their escalating confrontation

00:03:30.840 --> 00:03:34.340
with rival organizations, they're now
equipped with heavy arms.

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:37.410
Why would an organization like
that be protecting Yushiro?

00:03:37.410 --> 00:03:41.180
I can't say. But according to
Mr. Nishida's predictions,

00:03:41.180 --> 00:03:43.920
riots will break out in the Asian Veins,

00:03:43.920 --> 00:03:46.490
allowing us to deploy our
forces as peacekeepers.

00:03:46.490 --> 00:03:49.350
I'm certain we can use this chance
to find and secure your brother.

00:03:50.420 --> 00:03:54.520
Can I have one of the TA's deployed
in Kansai assigned to this?

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:57.300
To find your brother?

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:01.390
Well, considering how irreplaceable
your brother's abilities are...

00:04:02.000 --> 00:04:05.170
One TA company, comprised of four
units, will be deployed to Kansai.

00:04:05.170 --> 00:04:07.540
I'll have one of them dedicate its
operations to the search.

00:04:08.440 --> 00:04:09.640
I can't thank you enough.

00:04:09.640 --> 00:04:13.880
I'll have the lab forward Yushiro's
brain wave signature to you.

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:18.280
Yes, having that on hand should aid
the search effort tremendously.

00:04:18.280 --> 00:04:21.290
Now, in regards to what we can
anticipate America to do...

00:04:21.290 --> 00:04:23.410
I just received word from
a source yesterday.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:27.730
Everything is proceeding along the
lines that Mr. Nishida predicted.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:31.630
There's no question that grain prices
will shoot through the roof.

00:04:32.200 --> 00:04:34.970
What about the markets?

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:37.300
Today or tomorrow, the US government

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:41.830
should release their grain harvest
index forecast for this year.

00:04:42.740 --> 00:04:46.140
A run on the markets, leading
to a depression, will follow.

00:04:46.680 --> 00:04:48.080
Yes...

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:52.210
The opportunity has come for the
tree to shed its rotten fruit.

00:04:56.090 --> 00:04:58.720
What about Won?

00:04:58.720 --> 00:05:02.760
He hacked into the system for data on
the activities of council members.

00:05:02.760 --> 00:05:05.100
Was the prescribed amount
of information leaked?

00:05:05.100 --> 00:05:07.000
Yes, Sir, as you have instructed.

00:05:07.000 --> 00:05:10.100
Won should deem this information
useful for the Kyouwakai,

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:11.740
and act accordingly.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:14.970
Let us place our hopes on his actions.

00:05:16.280 --> 00:05:19.440
However, serious ramifications
will result

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:22.710
once the US Department of Agriculture
makes their report public.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:25.950
It would be prudent to avoid becoming
caught in the commotion

00:05:25.950 --> 00:05:27.950
that will erupt soon.

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:29.420
Yes, Sir.

00:05:32.220 --> 00:05:33.960
There's a riot starting!

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:35.430
Oh man, they've finally started!

00:05:38.630 --> 00:05:40.100
Let's go!

00:06:01.250 --> 00:06:02.780
We're not making much headway.

00:06:03.660 --> 00:06:05.560
Let's try increasing the culture
compound's concentration.

00:06:05.560 --> 00:06:07.860
Why don't we try injecting
some compound T?

00:06:08.460 --> 00:06:10.100
Why not?

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.930
We'll proceed in progressive stages.

00:06:11.930 --> 00:06:14.970
Mr. Kiyotsugu, someone from the
SSDF is here to see you.

00:06:14.970 --> 00:06:18.490
The SSDF? Oh, the stuff that my
brother asked me to handle.

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.340
Their data should be ready for pick
up at the information desk.

00:06:21.340 --> 00:06:22.410
Let them know that.

00:06:22.410 --> 00:06:23.080
Yes, Sir.

00:06:23.080 --> 00:06:23.910
You're handing over data to the SSDF?
Yes, Sir.

00:06:23.910 --> 00:06:25.280
You're handing over data to the SSDF?

00:06:25.280 --> 00:06:27.750
No, this is about the monoyose data.

00:06:27.750 --> 00:06:29.750
It doesn't have anything
to do with this.

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:32.340
Now, about the solution
ratio of compound T...

00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.190
What's all this about?

00:06:38.190 --> 00:06:40.290
They make us stand-by at this
place for over a month,

00:06:40.290 --> 00:06:42.790
and now all of a sudden they
tell us to ship back home.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:44.730
This really is rushed, isn't it?

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.870
The flight is in two hours.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:49.300
Isn't it part of our job
as SSDF soldiers

00:06:49.300 --> 00:06:51.240
to always remain ready for combat?

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:52.900
What happened to Colonel Hayakawa?

00:06:52.900 --> 00:06:54.910
The Colonel went to the Comm Center
just after the orders were issued,

00:06:54.910 --> 00:06:57.030
and he hasn't returned yet.

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:03.210
Something is about to begin?

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:10.460
To summon me while I'm at work...

00:07:10.460 --> 00:07:13.020
Let's keep this brief.

00:07:13.020 --> 00:07:15.890
I need to return to Ichigaya
as soon as possible.

00:07:15.890 --> 00:07:19.430
Uncle, I'm the master of
the house of Gowa.

00:07:19.430 --> 00:07:23.370
I believe I should expect a certain
degree of respect in this position.

00:07:23.370 --> 00:07:27.400
I don't care how you came to be
the master of this household.

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:30.880
Since this all followed the protocols
of the Gowa Family,

00:07:30.880 --> 00:07:33.450
I am not one to object to it.

00:07:33.450 --> 00:07:36.880
But I suggest you be content knowing
you possess vast power.

00:07:37.550 --> 00:07:41.650
I am not arrogant enough to demand
respect or reverence.

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:44.220
Dear Uncle, all I wish from you

00:07:44.220 --> 00:07:47.990
is the cooperation due the leader
of the Gowa Family.

00:07:47.990 --> 00:07:50.790
Cooperation? What are
you talking about?

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:54.530
Do you insist on playing
the fool, Uncle?

00:07:56.170 --> 00:07:57.800
You can't...

00:07:57.800 --> 00:08:03.000
You don't intend to become a hermit
like our brother Gi-Ichiro, do you?

00:08:03.910 --> 00:08:05.940
He was merely driven out

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:10.210
because his younger brother stole his
position as head of the Gowa.

00:08:10.850 --> 00:08:12.780
He did not become a
hermit intentionally.

00:08:13.890 --> 00:08:15.250
Kazukiyo,

00:08:15.250 --> 00:08:20.590
I realize that you are an integral
part of this plot that intends

00:08:20.590 --> 00:08:23.720
to shake Japan from its
very foundations.

00:08:24.660 --> 00:08:26.100
Of course I am.

00:08:26.100 --> 00:08:28.900
Dear Uncle, you must be
just as aware as I am.

00:08:29.470 --> 00:08:32.400
No matter how high a position we
may secure in the public world,

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.200
we are still Gowa.

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:36.430
That's all that matters to us.

00:08:37.040 --> 00:08:38.910
Kazukiyo,

00:08:38.910 --> 00:08:41.880
what do you intend to bring about
for the Gowa Family?

00:08:41.880 --> 00:08:43.720
I intend to return the Gowa

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:47.220
to their rightful position and
restore their proper nature.

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:48.990
Restore it to what?!

00:08:48.990 --> 00:08:50.420
The kugutsu...

00:08:50.420 --> 00:08:52.320
Puppeteers...

00:08:52.320 --> 00:08:55.320
That is what it means to be a Gowa.

00:08:58.360 --> 00:09:00.630
Is that information reliable?

00:09:01.200 --> 00:09:04.870
This is all information that was
gathered from our sources in

00:09:04.870 --> 00:09:07.040
the upper management of America's
largest grain corporations.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:10.470
And when will America
announce this policy?

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:15.980
Most likely early this evening.
Early tomorrow morning Japan time.

00:09:15.980 --> 00:09:19.280
Once this policy is announced, the
domestic and foreign grain markets,

00:09:19.280 --> 00:09:21.750
will go haywire, triggering
a financial panic.

00:09:21.750 --> 00:09:26.060
We already have riots breaking
out daily in the Asian Veins.

00:09:26.060 --> 00:09:29.290
Once the food shortages start...

00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:32.260
Actually, shortages aren't needed
for the situation to explode.

00:09:32.260 --> 00:09:34.200
Once people are touched
by the sensation of fear,

00:09:34.200 --> 00:09:37.570
it will compel them to take part in a
riot not seen in Japan in ages.

00:09:38.270 --> 00:09:41.140
Currently, there are already
500,000 illegal immigrants

00:09:41.140 --> 00:09:43.540
occupying the Veins around Japan.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.440
If a massive nationwide riot
were to break out now,

00:09:45.440 --> 00:09:48.410
we can expect over 100,000 casualties.

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:51.250
Damage will likely exceed
thirty billion yen.

00:09:51.250 --> 00:09:52.880
If we do nothing,

00:09:52.880 --> 00:09:56.860
this hypothetical situation
will become a reality.

00:09:56.860 --> 00:09:58.960
We can expect harsh criticism from
the international community

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:01.520
for lack of an effective prevention
and response policy.

00:10:02.390 --> 00:10:05.560
Please, you must authorize SSDF
peacekeeping operations.

00:10:06.100 --> 00:10:07.830
A courageous decision on your part

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.430
will ensure that our citizens will
escape largely unscathed.

00:10:16.240 --> 00:10:20.040
I see, he signed the
authorization document.

00:10:20.780 --> 00:10:22.410
At last, we are almost there.

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:25.680
In a few hours, the rapid economic
collapse will begin.

00:10:25.680 --> 00:10:29.350
I just received word from
General Gowa.

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.090
He states that he intends
to cooperate with us.

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:33.960
I see.

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:36.090
Be that as it may, the die
has been cast.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:40.800
We can only pray that when the
dawn greets us this morning

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.270
Japan will awaken from
its long slumber.

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:54.580
Today, the US Department of
Agriculture has revealed

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:56.720
in the annual grain harvest
forecast that

00:10:56.720 --> 00:11:00.170
this year's projected levels will fall
below 40% of the standard.

00:11:00.990 --> 00:11:01.050
With this devastating news
being released,

00:11:01.050 --> 00:11:02.550
This is not good.
With this devastating news
being released,

00:11:02.550 --> 00:11:03.320
With this devastating news
being released,

00:11:03.320 --> 00:11:06.590
A record 500 point surge shocked
the grain exchange market,

00:11:07.130 --> 00:11:09.530
forcing the Chicago Mercantile to
suspend trading at 3 o'clock.

00:11:09.530 --> 00:11:11.100
Currently, the market remains closed

00:11:11.100 --> 00:11:14.200
and a time has yet to be determined
for market to reopen.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.690
Furthermore, this latest
report from the USDA

00:11:17.400 --> 00:11:23.040
is having a severe impact on the
global grains exchange market,

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:26.030
prompting many calls for effective
policy by the government.

00:11:31.350 --> 00:11:33.490
Geez, we finally get to Tokyo,

00:11:33.490 --> 00:11:36.180
and now they tell us to head
to the experimental center.

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.790
They say we're taking off
in fifteen minutes.

00:11:38.790 --> 00:11:40.460
Okay.

00:11:40.460 --> 00:11:41.930
Is something the matter?

00:11:41.930 --> 00:11:44.700
The price of wheat went up
twenty dollars per bushel.

00:11:44.700 --> 00:11:46.260
And this year's global wheat stock

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:50.170
is 60% below the minimum safe
standards set by the FAO.

00:11:50.170 --> 00:11:51.700
The FAO?

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:55.010
The Food and Agriculture Organization
of the United Nations.

00:11:55.010 --> 00:11:56.570
How did you know that?

00:11:56.570 --> 00:11:58.180
It says right there.

00:11:58.180 --> 00:12:00.270
Oh, I see now.

00:12:06.720 --> 00:12:09.080
I wonder what we're going to do if
they scale back wheat imports?

00:12:09.990 --> 00:12:12.350
This is the season when
pizza tastes the best.

00:12:13.220 --> 00:12:14.710
Oh, yeah, I see.

00:12:15.290 --> 00:12:16.780
Hey, we're heading out!

00:12:20.330 --> 00:12:21.300
How was it?

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:21.830
No chance! Those Ryuka bastards
knew about this ahead of time!
How was it?

00:12:21.830 --> 00:12:24.670
No chance! Those Ryuka bastards
knew about this ahead of time!

00:12:24.670 --> 00:12:27.140
That's why they kept ignoring
the market price.

00:12:27.140 --> 00:12:28.940
But what about the store?

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.510
Can't you open the store
and serve people?

00:12:30.510 --> 00:12:33.170
Even if we wanted to, we
have nothing to sell.

00:12:33.880 --> 00:12:36.050
Then how are the people going to...

00:12:36.050 --> 00:12:39.710
I know those Ryuka bastards planned
on crushing us when this hit!

00:12:40.390 --> 00:12:43.090
Look, get this word
out to everyone.

00:12:43.090 --> 00:12:44.750
Tell them to just stay indoors.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.790
Following the announcement
by the USDA,

00:12:49.790 --> 00:12:51.300
numerous people have
rushed this morning

00:12:51.300 --> 00:12:53.360
to their neighborhood supermarket
and retailers all over Japan.

00:12:53.360 --> 00:12:55.900
There are reports of people
angered over the decision

00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.990
of some retailers to
withhold their inventory.

00:12:58.700 --> 00:13:00.670
The police are taking this
situation very seriously,

00:13:00.670 --> 00:13:03.540
deploying units in riot
gear to calm people,

00:13:03.540 --> 00:13:06.530
but tense situations persist
in numerous areas.

00:13:07.850 --> 00:13:10.920
Yes, well they released this just as
the pre-harvest months began.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:13.490
America certainly made this news
public at the worst possible time.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:16.250
Now it's only a matter of the Prime
Minister making the order public.

00:13:16.250 --> 00:13:19.590
Agreed. The masses are
a weak creature.

00:13:19.590 --> 00:13:21.660
Unless there is some powerful
force driving them,

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:24.100
at the slightest sign of
forceful suppression,

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:25.660
they fall apart very quickly.

00:13:25.660 --> 00:13:29.570
But you also know that one gunshot
can change everything instantly.

00:13:30.100 --> 00:13:33.970
That gunshot is the most terrifying
sound to the government,

00:13:33.970 --> 00:13:37.530
but nobody in the government
cares to realize this fact.

00:13:40.880 --> 00:13:43.720
You were in the position
of protecting Japan,

00:13:43.720 --> 00:13:46.450
and yet you invited that first
gunshot to be unleashed.

00:13:46.450 --> 00:13:48.450
It was an inevitable step to take.

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:51.060
To exterminate the violence
that lurks in the darkness,

00:13:51.060 --> 00:13:53.250
we must let it explode so
that it reveals itself fully.

00:13:54.590 --> 00:13:58.460
And yet you yourself are resorting to
violence through armed forces.

00:13:59.300 --> 00:14:01.600
I suppose you could say that.

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.770
But is it not also true that, in essence,

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:08.570
armed force is the only means by
which high ideals may be realized?

00:14:10.580 --> 00:14:12.840
The means by which high
ideals may be realized...

00:14:13.710 --> 00:14:15.180
But Mr. Hirokawa,

00:14:15.850 --> 00:14:18.250
the moment you resort
to those means,

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:20.950
don't your ideals transform
into a fragile mirage?

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:24.390
It seems that the tense confrontations

00:14:24.390 --> 00:14:26.420
between the police and citizens
that started this morning,

00:14:26.420 --> 00:14:28.990
have escalated to become
a full-scale riot.

00:14:28.990 --> 00:14:31.400
While details are still sketchy...

00:14:31.400 --> 00:14:33.300
So, what's the situation
with the riots?

00:14:33.300 --> 00:14:35.700
Where and in what magnitude
are these taking place?

00:14:38.240 --> 00:14:40.730
In many areas that situation is
starting to calm down, but...

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:44.310
The 8th District and the
12th District in Kanto,

00:14:44.310 --> 00:14:46.950
and the 6th District in Osaka...

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:49.950
You cannot even estimate how long
before things are under control?

00:14:49.950 --> 00:14:52.280
Some of those rioting are armed
with heavy weapons,

00:14:52.280 --> 00:14:55.220
and my men are not equipped nor
trained against, making it...

00:14:55.220 --> 00:14:57.090
Nearly impossible for the police
to regain control, you say?

00:14:58.020 --> 00:15:00.180
Just as Colonel Hirokawa predicted.

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:04.530
Understood. If the situation cannot be
contained by our police force,

00:15:04.530 --> 00:15:06.050
we have no other alternative.

00:15:06.730 --> 00:15:08.800
I am ordering the SSDF to conduct
peacekeeping operations!

00:15:08.800 --> 00:15:12.340
But Sir, it'll take time before our
forces can be of any use.

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.870
I already had the units
placed in position.

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:18.110
Already? How could they already be?

00:15:18.110 --> 00:15:19.880
There was the affair with the rioting.

00:15:19.880 --> 00:15:21.010
I took the initiative to have them

00:15:21.010 --> 00:15:23.040
stationed in appropriate locations
as part of a contingency plan.

00:15:25.780 --> 00:15:28.350
Bulletin from headquarters.
Initiate all operations.

00:15:28.350 --> 00:15:30.090
All units, deploy to designated areas
for deterrence operations.

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:32.820
Roger! Message to transporters,

00:15:32.820 --> 00:15:35.550
inform them that we are to initiate
operations by the Plan B scenario.

00:15:47.370 --> 00:15:50.540
Third platoon has been surrounded
by rioters and can't retreat!

00:15:50.540 --> 00:15:52.010
Where are our fire teams?

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:55.100
They're pinned down! They can't
get past the machine gun fire!

00:15:57.080 --> 00:15:59.350
Damn, where are our reinforcements?

00:16:07.760 --> 00:16:11.230
A platoon, charge ahead and
suppress blocks A through D.

00:16:11.230 --> 00:16:14.630
B platoon, remain in place
and provide rear support.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.100
Gustav 1, roger that.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:20.870
That's the SSDF's robot!

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:24.080
Just look at what those wackos
are throwing in!

00:16:24.080 --> 00:16:25.980
All units, load plastic warheads.

00:16:25.980 --> 00:16:27.950
Begin suppressive fire as necessary.

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:32.920
Hey, are you hurt?

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:34.910
No, I'm all right.

00:16:35.490 --> 00:16:37.090
Plastic?

00:16:37.090 --> 00:16:39.220
I've completed analysis of
their combat tactics.

00:16:39.220 --> 00:16:40.990
Hostiles are armed with
four machine guns,

00:16:40.990 --> 00:16:42.960
as well as anti-tank missiles.

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:46.060
Enemy moving to reinforce.
Point two-one to two-two.

00:16:46.060 --> 00:16:49.800
Gustav 2 take control of the final
pocket of resistance with Gustav 1.

00:16:49.800 --> 00:16:53.240
Report from the 3rd Company
deployed in the North Block.

00:16:53.240 --> 00:16:55.000
Confirming missile attack.

00:16:55.910 --> 00:16:57.370
BA Drive.

00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.010
Amazing! What kind of
a weapon is that?

00:17:05.680 --> 00:17:08.290
Program A1 completed.
Moving on to A2.

00:17:08.290 --> 00:17:09.650
Roger.

00:17:09.650 --> 00:17:09.790
Gustav 1, 2, 3, proceed to
suppression area 2.
Roger.

00:17:09.790 --> 00:17:12.990
Gustav 1, 2, 3, proceed to
suppression area 2.

00:17:12.990 --> 00:17:16.650
Gustav 4, begin operation 2 as
dictated by operation itinerary.

00:17:17.500 --> 00:17:21.000
This is Focke 1, we'll take over
administration of Gustav 4.

00:17:21.000 --> 00:17:22.000
We don't have a lot of time.

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:24.200
The acquisition of the target is
dependent on your detection.

00:17:24.200 --> 00:17:27.910
I understand. But if they remain
inside buildings,

00:17:27.910 --> 00:17:30.680
we won't be able to detect them
with thermograph sensors.

00:17:30.680 --> 00:17:32.770
At the very least, we need
them at a window sill.

00:17:33.480 --> 00:17:34.810
With commotion like this going on,

00:17:34.810 --> 00:17:39.150
any normal person would stick their
head out trying to get a glimpse.

00:17:39.150 --> 00:17:41.920
All we need you to find is
the building they're in.

00:17:41.920 --> 00:17:43.450
Leave the rest to us.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:44.920
Roger that.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:53.620
Damn! Yushiro, you stay put
for awhile, you got that?

00:17:59.500 --> 00:18:00.610
What's the deal?

00:18:00.610 --> 00:18:01.010
That's the sound of a SSDF helicopter.
What's the deal?

00:18:01.010 --> 00:18:02.640
That's the sound of a SSDF helicopter.

00:18:02.640 --> 00:18:03.940
The JSSDF?

00:18:03.940 --> 00:18:04.140
You were here after all!
The JSSDF?

00:18:04.140 --> 00:18:05.940
You were here after all!

00:18:05.940 --> 00:18:09.210
Mr. Won, the SSDF's coming
down main street.

00:18:09.210 --> 00:18:11.920
The SSDF? Not the Ryuka punks?

00:18:11.920 --> 00:18:13.920
Yeah, and what's more,

00:18:13.920 --> 00:18:19.060
the robot that fought overseas
suppressed the riot just like that.

00:18:19.060 --> 00:18:20.520
The TA did?

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:25.490
The Ryuka gang got beat up pretty
badly, and now they're headed here.

00:18:27.600 --> 00:18:30.170
There it is. So, that's the TA?

00:18:30.170 --> 00:18:31.440
Why would...

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:31.670
Wait, Yushiro!
Why would...

00:18:31.670 --> 00:18:33.100
Wait, Yushiro!

00:18:33.100 --> 00:18:35.370
You mentioned the chopper
overhead is the SSDF's.

00:18:36.170 --> 00:18:39.210
Are those equipped with detection
systems for human targets?

00:18:39.210 --> 00:18:41.340
Yes, they are equipped with
thermograph sensors.

00:18:42.480 --> 00:18:44.910
Mr. Won, how many TA's are there?

00:18:47.190 --> 00:18:48.320
One.

00:18:48.320 --> 00:18:48.690
I suspected as much.
One.

00:18:48.690 --> 00:18:49.890
I suspected as much.

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:51.360
What do you mean?

00:18:51.360 --> 00:18:54.330
TA's normally operate
in teams of four.

00:18:54.330 --> 00:18:56.430
If only one is walking about,

00:18:56.430 --> 00:18:58.600
then it must have been sent
separately from its main unit.

00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.800
Will it be able to detect you inside?

00:19:00.800 --> 00:19:04.200
TA's are equipped with individual
personal identification system.

00:19:04.200 --> 00:19:06.840
With its sensor systems linked
with the overhead helicopter,

00:19:06.840 --> 00:19:10.740
it can sweep a wide area rapidly
searching for specific individuals.

00:19:11.280 --> 00:19:13.710
But as long as we don't get
close to a window...

00:19:13.710 --> 00:19:16.080
All right, you make sure that you
keep your head down.

00:19:16.080 --> 00:19:17.820
Lee, I'm going to leave you
here just to be safe.

00:19:17.820 --> 00:19:19.350
Mr. Won, what do you intend to do?

00:19:19.350 --> 00:19:22.390
Don't worry about it. I just
want to get a good look.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:25.220
But if it gets close to here,
I'm going to blast away at it!

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:26.490
No...

00:19:26.490 --> 00:19:29.050
It's going to take a lot more than an
anti-tank rifle to defeat a TA.

00:19:30.900 --> 00:19:33.920
Yushiro, you piloted those
things, right?

00:19:37.300 --> 00:19:38.830
Does it have any weaknesses
I can exploit?

00:19:39.740 --> 00:19:41.840
In these circumstances, there's
little you can do.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:44.360
You need at least a tank
to stop a TA.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:46.780
But if the unit is moving
about on its own,

00:19:46.780 --> 00:19:50.740
damage to its optical sensors will
impede its ability to operate.

00:19:51.280 --> 00:19:53.550
The optical sensors? Got it!

00:20:09.100 --> 00:20:11.590
We're not detecting anything that
resembles what we're looking for.

00:20:12.140 --> 00:20:14.870
We don't have much time. If we can't
find anything within ten minutes,

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:16.530
we're going to call off
this operation.

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:32.560
Detecting Type Two!

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.020
Swing the camera around for a peek.

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:38.190
Target two has been acquired!
Relaying location data of target.

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:40.430
Go!

00:20:57.250 --> 00:20:59.120
What the...

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:02.790
Heart rate, pulse, dopamine receptor
rate, all at normal levels.

00:21:02.790 --> 00:21:05.260
Proceed with physical control
mode level D.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:06.720
Up!

00:21:10.090 --> 00:21:13.360
There's one on the move! They're
heading straight this way!

00:21:17.100 --> 00:21:18.570
Miharu!

00:21:36.520 --> 00:21:38.820
I have acquired the target.
Proceeding to secure it.

00:21:42.630 --> 00:21:44.090
Miharu!

00:21:51.940 --> 00:21:53.400
Backup B!

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:58.180
CB, Gustav 4 here. My optics
have been damaged.

00:21:58.180 --> 00:22:00.580
I can no longer use the automatic
target acquisition system.

00:22:00.580 --> 00:22:03.050
Requesting permission to
cease current mission.

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:04.780
Roger that Gustav 4.

00:22:04.780 --> 00:22:06.420
Best for you to come
back right away.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:07.880
Hurry back!

00:22:11.990 --> 00:22:14.560
Is that girl all right?

00:22:14.560 --> 00:22:16.580
Yes, but you, Mr. Won?

00:22:17.260 --> 00:22:19.100
Hey, I like this.

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:20.460
Moments where you lose yourself

00:22:20.460 --> 00:22:23.760
to the compulsion of wanting
to save someone...

00:22:29.970 --> 00:22:34.790
Hark

00:22:36.050 --> 00:22:41.340
It's time I journey

00:22:44.870 --> 00:22:52.010
Break apart my heart

00:22:52.180 --> 00:22:58.540
For crimson sadness

00:22:58.870 --> 00:23:06.050
Pours out from it

00:23:06.260 --> 00:23:09.970
I can only, oh

00:23:10.080 --> 00:23:13.160
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:13.250 --> 00:23:18.770
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:33.990 --> 00:23:37.870
I can only, oh

00:23:37.960 --> 00:23:41.020
Close my eyes, oh

00:23:41.090 --> 00:23:46.220
I pray, let this break apart

00:23:47.750 --> 00:23:54.200
I beg you, be by my side

00:24:01.930 --> 00:24:04.500
The mysteries of the ties that bind
people to one another...

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.640
Why do we encounter each other?

00:24:06.640 --> 00:24:08.540
Why do we protect one another?

00:24:08.540 --> 00:24:10.910
What guides us to do this?

00:24:10.910 --> 00:24:13.280
Farewells come all of a sudden.

00:24:13.280 --> 00:24:16.440
Mercilessly, barbarously,
and without reason.

00:24:17.010 --> 00:24:18.680
Led by righteousness

00:24:18.680 --> 00:24:21.120
A man dies, and I am witness
to his last breath

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:24.140
Mourning wails of anguish are
swallowed up by the dark sea

00:24:24.920 --> 00:24:28.790
Must we be made to accept
all this cruelty?
